  "body": "The _decimal character reference start state_ is used by the _numeric character reference state_ to reconsume the current character. The state itself then immediately switches to the _decimal character reference state_ or the _return state_ to (once more) reconsume the current character.\n\nThis immediate switching behavior makes the _decimal character reference start state_ hard to test, as no input will leave the tokenizer in the state. There is no other state that cannot be navigated to using a targeted input. Merging the state into the _numeric character reference state_ resolves this, without changing the behavior.\n\nThis PR is a follow-up of https://github.com/inikulin/parse5/pull/517/files#r854906380.\n\n\n<!--\n    This comment and the below content is programmatically generated.\n    You may add a comma-separated list of anchors you'd like a\n    direct link to below (e.g. #idl-serializers, #idl-sequence):\n\n    Don't remove this comment or modify anything below this line.\n    If you don't want a preview generated for this pull request,\n    just replace the whole of this comment's content by \"no preview\"\n    and remove what's below.\n-->\n***\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7841/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 21, 2022, 10:35 AM UTC (3083c96)\">/index.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7841/5448492...3083c96/index.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 21, 2022, 10:35 AM UTC (3083c96)\">diff</a> )\n<a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7841/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 21, 2022, 10:35 AM UTC (3083c96)\">/parsing.html</a>  ( <a href=\"https://whatpr.org/html/7841/5448492...3083c96/parsing.html\" title=\"Last updated on Apr 21, 2022, 10:35 AM UTC (3083c96)\">diff</a> )",
